block='''<h2 id="free-ipad-planner-download-check">Free iPad planner downloads: keep the editable and writing formats separate</h2><p>A blank PDF is a writing copy, not the editable data backup for a browser worksheet. For example, the <a href="/downloads/time-blocking-template.pdf" download>free two-page weekly time-blocking PDF</a> has a fixed 09:00–17:00 writing grid. Keep its blank original and annotate a copy in a compatible PDF app. It has no interactive calculations, linked tabs or reminders.</p><p>The separate <a href="/tools/time-blocking-template/">weekly time-blocking browser tool</a> accepts named blocks and checks gaps and overlaps. Its JSON backup reopens those editable inputs in that same tool; its CSV is a reviewed row export. Neither file becomes a Goodnotes PDF merely by renaming it. A browser print/PDF report is another static output, with saving controlled by your device's print dialog.</p><p>For any iPad workflow, test one harmless entry, close/reopen the correct working copy and verify how changes survive before relying on it. This format explanation is not a claim of native iPad-app support or a physical-device compatibility test. Compare the <a href="/journal/best-digital-planner-for-ipad/">iPad format guide</a> and each product's documented requirements.</p>'''
